[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Rousseau Gambit"]
[Variation "Rousseau Gambit: 4.Nxe5 Nxe5 5.Bxg8"]
[ECO "C50"]
[Character "gambit,tactical"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,hanging-piece"]
[Themes "piece-activity,f7-pressure"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 f5 4. Nxe5 { White grabs the pawn, but it costs a piece. The knight on e5 is not protected enough, and the f5 pawn has opened the g1-a7 and h4 lines against White. } 4... Nxe5 { Takes the knight. Black is now ahead in material, and White's bishop on c4 is attacked once the d-pawn moves. [%cal Gc6e5] }
5. Bxg8 (5. d4 5... Nxc4 6. O-O 6... d5) (5. Bb3 5... fxe4 6. Qh5+ 6... Ng6) (5. exf5 5... Nxc4 6. Qh5+ 6... g6 7. fxg6 7... Qe7+) (5. Qe2 5... Nxc4 6. Qxc4 6... d5) (5. Qh5+ 5... g6 6. Qe2 6... Nxc4 7. Qxc4 7... c6) (5. d3 5... Nxc4 6. dxc4 6... Bb4+) 5... Rxg8 { The rook takes the bishop. Black has won a knight for a pawn. } 6. O-O 6... fxe4 { Takes the pawn that White just left behind and opens the f-file towards White's king. } 7. d4 7... Ng6 { The knight steps out of the pawn's way and heads for the strong f4 and h4 squares. } 8. Nc3 (8. d5 8... Be7) 8... d5 { Fills the centre and keeps the e4 pawn safe. } 9. f3 9... Bd6 *
